    }","notes":"The probe calls deposit(100) after setup (paused flag 0, store_c length 1 from setLimits(1,1000000)). Candidate kept the guard block behind `if (msg.data.length - 4 >= 0x10)` and then unconditionally `revert()`; with a 4-byte selector plus one 32-byte arg the condition is true, so the guards pass but the trailing revert makes the call fail (step 0: candidate ok=false vs reference ok=true). Removed the length conditional and the trailing revert so the two observed guards run and the call returns successfully, matching reference ok=true with no return data and no logs; balanceOf/totalSupply/getStats deltas (1009 = 1000 mint + 9 fee-adjusted deposit... reference shows 0x44b=1099) are produced by the other units and are untouched here."}
